[{"_1":2},"llms/mdx",{"_3":4},"data","# Troubleshooting (/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/troubleshooting)\n\n\n\n<div className=\"lm-diff-ins lm-diff-block\">\n  Diagnose one operation at a time. Note the backend (`GET /updates/v1/capabilities` shows it), the endpoint, the HTTP status and the `err` text of the response body: errors are returned as `{\"err\": \"...\"}`. If your problem is not here, check [Limitations](/docs/platform/updates/limitations) first.\n</div>\n\n<div className=\"lm-diff-ins lm-diff-block\">\n  HTTP status codes [#http-status-codes]\n</div>\n\n<div className=\"lm-diff-ins lm-diff-block\">\n  | Status | Meaning                                                                                                                    |\n  | ------ | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n  | `400`  | The request or the current state of the resource does not allow the operation. The message says what to change.            |\n  | `403`  | A policy refuses the operation.                                                                                            |\n  | `404`  | The resource does not exist. Another group's launch also answers `404`.                                                    |\n  | `409`  | A conflicting operation is in progress, or the version is already built.                                                   |\n  | `413`  | A file is larger than `max_artifact_size_mb`.                                                                              |\n  | `500`  | An unexpected failure. Some validation errors still answer `500` (see below).                                              |\n  | `501`  | The active backend does not support the operation. Read the [capabilities](/docs/platform/updates/reference/capabilities). |\n</div>\n\n<div className=\"lm-diff-ins lm-diff-block\">\n  Starting the service [#starting-the-service]\n</div>\n\n<div className=\"lm-diff-ins lm-diff-block\">\n  | Symptom or message                                                            | Likely cause                                                                  | Fix                                                                                                                          |\n  | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n  | `docker compose up` fails with a network error                                | The `ota-net` network does not exist                                          | `docker network create ota-net`                                                                                              |\n  | Docker build cannot find `lamassuiot/core`                                    | The build context is not the parent of the checkout                           | Build with the context that contains `ota/`, `lamassuiot/core` and `lamassuiot/sdk`. `docker compose build updates` uses it. |\n  | The service ignores `OTA_CONFIG_FILE` and logs a warning                      | The file could not be loaded, so it fell back to `/etc/lamassuiot/config.yml` | Check the path and the YAML. In the image the fallback is the repository's developer configuration.                          |\n  | `workflow_file \"...\" must contain \"direct\"`                                   | `workflow_file` does not name the `direct` workflow                           | Point it at `wfx.workflow.dau.direct.yml` or a path containing `direct`.                                                     |\n  | `failed to list existing WFX workflows`                                       | `wfx_endpoint` is wrong or WFX is down                                        | Use the **management** port (`8081` inside the Compose network, `9081` on the host) and check that `custom-wfx` runs.        |\n  | Postgres reports that database `updates` does not exist                       | The database is not created by the service                                    | Create it (Docker Compose does it through `init.sql`).                                                                       |\n  | `mode is \"hawkbit\" but hawkbit.base_url is not configured`                    | Missing key                                                                   | Set `hawkbit.base_url`.                                                                                                      |\n  | `mode is \"hawkbit\" but storage (Postgres) is not configured`                  | `storage.hostname` is empty                                                   | Set the `storage` block.                                                                                                     |\n  | `S3 bucket \"x\" is not accessible at ...`                                      | Wrong bucket, endpoint or credentials, or the bucket does not exist           | Fix the `s3_*` keys of the block named in the error. The bucket must already exist.                                          |\n  | `local encryption key must be exactly 32 bytes`                               | `encryption.local_key` is not 32 bytes of hex                                 | Use 64 hex characters (`openssl rand -hex 32`).                                                                              |\n  | `could not configure leader election: the service account may not ... Leases` | The pod cannot use Leases and `leaderElection.mode` is `kubernetes`           | Grant the Role the chart provides (`serviceAccount.create: true`), or set `leaderElection.mode: database`.                   |\n  | `not running inside a Kubernetes cluster`                                     | `leader_election.mode: kubernetes` outside a cluster                          | Use empty (auto) or `database`.                                                                                              |\n  | `builds.presign: ...` or `hawkbit.artifact_store.presign: ...`                | The presigned-download settings of that block are invalid                     | See [Downloads and presigned URLs](#downloads-and-presigned-urls).                                                           |\n  | The hawkBit container exits                                                   | S3 storage is selected for hawkBit and the bucket is unreachable              | Fix the S3 settings, or use `HAWKBIT_ARTIFACT_STORAGE=fs`. hawkBit never falls back to local disk silently.                  |\n  | `/health` answers but WFX calls fail                                          | `/health` does not check dependencies                                         | Check `wfx_endpoint` and that WFX is running.                                                                                |\n  | Debug output shows secrets                                                    | `app.logs.level: debug` prints the configuration                              | Use `info`. See [Security](/docs/platform/updates/security).                                                                 |\n</div>\n\n<div className=\"lm-diff-ins lm-diff-block\">\n  API calls [#api-calls]\n</div>\n\n<div className=\"lm-diff-ins lm-diff-block\">\n  | Symptom or message                                                                                             | Likely cause                                                                                 | Fix                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    |\n  | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n  | `501 Not Implemented`                                                                                          | The active backend does not support the operation                                            | Read `GET /updates/v1/capabilities`. In `hawkbit` mode, `POST .../swu` and `.../package` always answer `501`: build the modules in the catalog.                                                                                                                                                                                        |\n  | `409` `update pack version X is already built; create a new version ...`                                       | You changed a built version                                                                  | Native mode: `POST .../new` with `{\"version\":\"x.y.z\"}` greater than the current one, then upload the sw-description again (it is not carried over) and give any re-uploaded artifact a higher `version`. `hawkbit` mode: see the next row.                                                                                             |\n  | `hawkbit mode: cannot ... here — a software module linked to a distribution set is frozen` (`400`)             | Pack-scoped edits are refused in `hawkbit` mode                                              | Unlink the module, change and build it in the catalog, link it again. Or release a new version of the module and create a pack from it under another name: pack names are unique per group, and an `os` module cannot be swapped on an existing pack. See [hawkBit mode](/docs/platform/updates/hawkbit-mode#create-and-build-a-pack). |\n  | `409` `... is being built or changed by another request; retry when it finishes`                               | Two builds, or a build and a change, on the same pack or module                              | Wait and retry. The lock is released when the operation ends or fails.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                 |\n  | `409` on create                                                                                                | A pack with that name exists in the group                                                    | Pick another name.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                     |\n  | `413` `file \"x\" is N MiB; the maximum upload size is M MiB`                                                    | The file exceeds `max_artifact_size_mb`                                                      | Raise it, and the limits of every proxy in front. See [Operations](/docs/platform/updates/operations#upload-size-and-proxies). A proxy answering `413` with its own body (for example nginx's default 1 MiB) is the proxy, not the service.                                                                                            |\n  | Upload `400` mentioning content that contradicts the filename                                                  | A file named `.swu` is not a SWU                                                             | Upload a real `.swu`, or rename the file.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                              |\n  | Artifact upload fails with `500` and `version X must be greater than the current latest version`               | Artifact names are global, and a name can only be reused with a higher `version`             | Give the new file a higher `version`, or a new artifact name.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          |\n  | `Cannot create launch: update pack 'x' has not been built yet` (`400`)                                         | The pack is still a draft                                                                    | Build it first.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                        |\n  | `Cannot create launch: update pack \"x\" is per-device encrypted and only N of M devices have a package` (`400`) | Some devices have no key                                                                     | Assign the missing keys and build again. There is no override.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                         |\n  | `approval_threshold and error_threshold must be between 0 and 100`                                             | Thresholds are percentages                                                                   | Use `0`-`100`.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                         |\n  | `launch X is paused; resume it first` (`400`)                                                                  | The launch was paused                                                                        | Call `resume`.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                         |\n  | `test device X cannot act as this group's canary: device X does not exist` (`hawkbit` mode)                    | The canary check runs before the group's devices exist in hawkBit                            | Run a dry run without `test_device_id` first (`POST .../launch?dry_run=true`), which registers the devices as targets.                                                                                                                                                                                                                 |\n  | The device registry or KMS answers `401`                                                                       | The service always sends `X-Principal-ID: admin-mode`, and the gateway in between rejects it | Point `dms_endpoint` and `kms_endpoint` at the internal service addresses, or allow that header.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                       |\n</div>\n\n<div className=\"lm-diff-ins lm-diff-block\">\n  Builds [#builds]\n</div>\n\n<div className=\"lm-diff-ins lm-diff-block\">\n  | Symptom or message                                                                                      | Likely cause                                                                             | Fix                                                                                                                                  |\n  | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n  | `no sw-descriptor uploaded for update pack \"x\" vN`                                                      | The version has no sw-description (each version needs its own)                           | Upload it.                                                                                                                           |\n  | `failed to read binaries directory` or `binaries directory is empty`                                    | `native` mode: nothing was staged, because the build body has no `selected_artifact_ids` | Pass the artifact IDs. See the [publish guide](/docs/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out).                                  |\n  | `swugenerator failed: exit status N`                                                                    | The tool rejected its input. Its own message is in the service log                       | Check the sw-description, the file names it references, the algorithm spelling (`aes-256-gcm`, hyphens required) and the key length. |\n  | `signing requested but sign_script_path/kms endpoint are not configured`                                | A `.swu` was asked to be signed without both settings                                    | Set `sign_script_path` and `kms_endpoint`.                                                                                           |\n  | `signing requires key id, algorithm and certificate together`                                           | A partial signature request                                                              | Send all three `signature_*` fields.                                                                                                 |\n  | `failed to sign version manifest: the KMS did not return a PKCS7/CMS signature`                         | The KMS answered with a bare signature                                                   | Use a KMS version that returns CMS. See [Signing and encryption](/docs/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#signing).             |\n  | `symKMS SDK client is not configured`                                                                   | `symkms_endpoint` is empty                                                               | Set it. In `hawkbit` mode also set the `symkms` block so the routes exist.                                                           |\n  | `failed to fetch key \"k\" via symKMS`                                                                    | Wrong key ID or `user`, or the endpoint points at another instance                       | The key belongs to its `user_id`; `symkms_endpoint` must be this instance's own address and port.                                    |\n  | Per-device build fails mentioning `encrypted = true`                                                    | No artifact in the sw-description is marked `encrypted = true;`                          | Mark the artifacts to encrypt.                                                                                                       |\n  | `no devices found for DMS X` or `none of the N devices ... have a key assigned for firmware-encryption` | The group has no devices in the registry, or none has a key                              | Check the group in Lamassu IoT and `dms_endpoint`; assign `firmware-encryption` keys.                                                |\n  | `hawkbit mode: this deployment has no SWU builder configured` (`501`)                                   | `swugenerator_path` is empty                                                             | Set it, or upload a prebuilt `.swu` module.                                                                                          |\n  | `hawkbit mode: this deployment has no SymKMS configured` or `... no KMS endpoint configured` (`501`)    | Encryption or signing asked without `symkms_endpoint` or `kms_endpoint`                  | Set them.                                                                                                                            |\n  | `software module \"x\" ... is N MB and encrypting it needs about M MB in memory`                          | `build_memory_limit_mb` refuses the build                                                | Sign without encrypting, split the file, or raise the limit together with the pod's memory.                                          |\n  | `... is already built; ... release a new version of it to build again`                                  | A build replaces the module's input files                                                | Create a new version of the module.                                                                                                  |\n</div>\n\n<div className=\"lm-diff-ins lm-diff-block\">\n  Downloads and presigned URLs [#downloads-and-presigned-urls]\n</div>\n\n<div className=\"lm-diff-ins lm-diff-block\">\n  | Symptom or message                                                | Likely cause                                                                                                                                                                                                     | Fix                                                                                                                                                                                               |\n  | ----------------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n  | `404` `SWU not available for device D on pack \"x\" vN`             | The pack is per-device encrypted and has no package for that device (its key was missing at build time, or the pack inherited per-device mode from an earlier version), or the build file is gone from the store | Assign the device's key and build a new version. To avoid inheriting, use a separate pack for each encryption variant (see [Limitations](/docs/platform/updates/limitations#packs-and-versions)). |\n  | Startup: `presign needs its own credential`                       | `presign` is enabled without a signing credential                                                                                                                                                                | Set `presign.access_key_id[_file]` and `secret_access_key[_file]`, a read-only pair.                                                                                                              |\n  | Startup: `the presign credential can WRITE`                       | The signing credential has write access                                                                                                                                                                          | Give it a read-only policy on the objects it serves.                                                                                                                                              |\n  | Startup: `presign signs with the storage's own credential`        | Same key as the storage                                                                                                                                                                                          | Create a separate read-only key.                                                                                                                                                                  |\n  | Startup: `the store does not accept the presign credential`       | The store does not know the key, or the signature does not match                                                                                                                                                 | Create the user in the store; check region and endpoint.                                                                                                                                          |\n  | Startup: `presign cannot be combined with client-side encryption` | `encryption.type` is not `none` on that block                                                                                                                                                                    | Use store-side encryption, or disable `presign`.                                                                                                                                                  |\n  | Startup: `presign.public_endpoint must be an http(s) origin`      | The value has no scheme, or has a path                                                                                                                                                                           | Use an origin such as `https://updates.example.com`.                                                                                                                                              |\n  | The device gets `403` from the store after the `302`              | The URL expired before the device started the GET, the signed `Host` is not what the device used (`public_endpoint` wrong), the signing key cannot read that prefix, or clocks differ                            | Retry (a fresh URL is issued per request); check `ttl`, `public_endpoint` and the key's policy.                                                                                                   |\n  | Downloads stream through the service despite `presign`            | A `HEAD` request, an artifact download by ID in `native` mode, a store without `presign` for that block, or the signing failed (logged)                                                                          | Only builds in `native` mode and the S3 plugin objects in `hawkbit` mode are redirected.                                                                                                          |\n</div>\n\n<div className=\"lm-diff-ins lm-diff-block\">\n  Updates not reaching devices [#updates-not-reaching-devices]\n</div>\n\n<div className=\"lm-diff-ins lm-diff-block\">\n  | Symptom                                                                             | Likely cause                                                                                                      | Fix                                                                                                                                         |\n  | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n  | Devices cannot download the `.swu` (`native` mode)                                  | `update_domain` is not reachable from the device, or is not the full `.../updates/v1/` base with a trailing slash | Use an address the device can resolve. The Helm chart default lacks `/updates`.                                                             |\n  | `hawkbit` mode: a device gets `401` from DDI                                        | hawkBit refuses devices that do not authenticate                                                                  | Enable and use a hawkBit device authenticator. See [hawkBit mode](/docs/platform/updates/hawkbit-mode#device-authentication-in-production). |\n  | `hawkbit` mode: a device gets `429`                                                 | hawkBit's own DoS filter, which limits how often a device may call it                                             | Slow the polling and feedback of the device.                                                                                                |\n  | `hawkbit` mode: the launch stays `running` with no progress                         | The devices never contacted hawkBit, or they poll a different hawkBit                                             | Check which hawkBit the devices poll, and that the targets exist. A rollout group cannot advance until its devices poll.                    |\n  | `hawkbit` mode: devices are not found in the group                                  | `dms_endpoint` is not set, so groups are the `group:<id>` target tags                                             | Set `dms_endpoint`, or tag the targets.                                                                                                     |\n  | A `phased` launch stays at `CREATED` (`native` mode)                                | In the `phased` workflow some steps are made by WFX or an operator                                                | Confirm them through WFX, or use `direct`.                                                                                                  |\n  | A `non-swu` launch shows SWU states (`native` mode)                                 | It was created with `workflow_type: direct`                                                                       | Use `download-install`.                                                                                                                     |\n  | The device installs and shows the old version                                       | The payload version was not changed                                                                               | Bump the version before building.                                                                                                           |\n  | The device ignores new deployments                                                  | SWUpdate keeps the update state of an earlier install as pending test (`ustate=1`) and refuses a new one          | Confirm or reset the device's update state. This is a device setting, not a service one.                                                    |\n  | The device rejects the `.swu` and the error mentions decryption or an invalid image | The `.swu` is unsigned while the device requires a signature, or the signature is not CMS                         | Sign it with a KMS that returns CMS. A signature failure can be reported as an encryption error.                                            |\n  | The device fails to decrypt                                                         | The key used to build differs from the device's key, or the algorithm spelling differs                            | Use the same key and algorithm. Check the assignment in SymKMS.                                                                             |\n</div>\n\n<div className=\"lm-diff-ins lm-diff-block\">\n  Scaling and background work [#scaling-and-background-work]\n</div>\n\n<div className=\"lm-diff-ins lm-diff-block\">\n  | Symptom                                                  | Likely cause                                                                | Fix                                                                                                                                                |\n  | -------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n  | Pods cannot start on different nodes                     | The `ReadWriteOnce` volume (both modes while `persistence.enabled` is true) | Set `persistence.enabled: false` and move `artifacts`, `builds` and `symkms` to S3. See [Operations](/docs/platform/updates/operations#scale-out). |\n  | Campaign batches never advance (`native` mode)           | Leader election is failing, or WFX events are not arriving                  | Check the Leases and the RBAC, or set `leaderElection.mode: database`. The log line `leadership acquired` appears on the leader.                   |\n  | Scheduled launches never start (`native` mode)           | The same background work, which runs on the leader                          | As above.                                                                                                                                          |\n  | Per-device builds are slow                               | The CPU limit                                                               | Raise it. See [Resource sizing](/docs/platform/updates/operations#resource-sizing).                                                                |\n  | The pod is killed during an upload or an encrypted build | Memory limit, or the temporary disk is full                                 | Size memory for the largest file you encrypt, and give `TMPDIR` room.                                                                              |\n</div>\n\n<div className=\"lm-diff-ins lm-diff-block\">\n  Getting more information [#getting-more-information]\n</div>\n\n<div className=\"lm-diff-ins lm-diff-block\">\n  * Raise `app.logs.level` to `debug`, but remember that it prints secrets.\n  * `GET /updates/v1/capabilities` shows the active backend and what it supports.\n  * Each replica logs which one leads (`leadership acquired`, `is the leader, standing by`).\n  * In `hawkbit` mode, inspect what the service created through hawkBit's Management API (port `8090` in Compose, with the Basic Auth credentials of the configuration). Each hawkBit instance has its own data: query the one named in `hawkbit.base_url`.\n</div>\n"]
